## Where to call Jev

| Route | Model ID | How |
|---|---|---|
| **TypeSafe direct** | `jev-1.13.0` / `jev-latest` | `POST api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone` with the official SDKs |
| **[Vercel AI Gateway](https://vercel.com/ai-gateway/models/jev)** {{n:https://vercel.com/ai-gateway/models/jev}} | `typesafe-ai/jev` | AI SDK 7 `experimental_evaluate` / [`@ai-sdk/typesafe-ai`](https://ai-sdk.dev/providers/ai-sdk-providers/typesafe-ai). Noul is called `boolean` here. |
| **[Cloudflare Workers AI](https://developers.cloudflare.com/ai/models/typesafe/jev/)** {{n:https://developers.cloudflare.com/ai/models/typesafe/jev}} | `typesafe/jev` | `env.AI.run(...)` |
| **[OpenRouter](https://openrouter.ai/typesafe/jev-1.13)** | `typesafe/jev-1.13` | Decisions API (`/api/alpha/decisions`), not chat completions. There is also a [Jev Router](https://openrouter.ai/typesafe/jev-router). |
| **[Netlify AI Gateway](https://docs.netlify.com/build/ai-gateway/overview/)** · **[LiteLLM](https://docs.litellm.ai/docs/pass_through/typesafe)** | `jev-latest` | The official JS SDK from Netlify Functions · a pass-through proxy |

Field names and schemas differ between routes, so porting is not a URL swap. The [full matrix, with gotchas](docs/what-is-jev.md#where-you-can-call-jev-access-routes) covers them.

