### Coding-agent tooling

The largest cluster in the ecosystem. It covers Claude Code, Codex, Pi, Hermes, OpenCode and Cursor.

**Context compaction and pruning.** This is contested, so read the [evidence](docs/evidence.md#negative-and-null-results) first.
- [tamaratran/fast-jev-compaction](https://github.com/tamaratran/fast-jev-compaction) {{s:tamaratran/fast-jev-compaction}} — The most-starred project in the category. It replaces Claude Code's compaction summary with keep/drop decisions per tool call, and kept content stays verbatim. It began as a [viral demo](https://x.com/tamarajtran/status/2100694549362553153).
- [tamaratran/jev-pruner](https://github.com/tamaratran/jev-pruner) {{s:tamaratran/jev-pruner}} — Trims long Bash output before the model sees it.
- [GhalebDweikat/winnow](https://github.com/GhalebDweikat/winnow) {{s:GhalebDweikat/winnow}} — A calibrated context sieve with stub/recall pointers. It falls back to the system-one-adapter when Jev is unreachable.
- [kunchenguid/compact-adviser](https://github.com/kunchenguid/compact-adviser) {{s:kunchenguid/compact-adviser}} — Asks "is this a safe moment to compact?"
- [joelhooks/pi-fast-jev-compaction](https://github.com/joelhooks/pi-fast-jev-compaction) {{s:joelhooks/pi-fast-jev-compaction}} · [leonaaardob/fast-dev-compaction](https://github.com/leonaaardob/fast-dev-compaction) {{s:leonaaardob/fast-dev-compaction}} · [compozy/yoshi](https://github.com/compozy/yoshi) {{s:compozy/yoshi}} — Ports to Pi and Codex, and a pruning proxy.

**Model and effort routing.** Route at session boundaries and run in shadow mode first.
- [gargpratyush/jev-router](https://github.com/gargpratyush/jev-router) {{s:gargpratyush/jev-router}} — Routes Claude Code and Codex to the cheapest capable model.
- [0xNatoshi/jev-codex-router](https://github.com/0xNatoshi/jev-codex-router) {{s:0xNatoshi/jev-codex-router}} — Per-turn model, reasoning-effort and speed routing for Codex (~60% savings on a 237-turn backtest).
- [BillionsBobby/JevRouter](https://github.com/BillionsBobby/JevRouter) {{s:BillionsBobby/JevRouter}} — One candidate set covering models, tools, subagents and skills.
- [ruban-24/switchboard](https://github.com/ruban-24/switchboard) {{s:ruban-24/switchboard}} · [adarshmishra07/jcm-router](https://github.com/adarshmishra07/jcm-router) {{s:adarshmishra07/jcm-router}} · [xinyao27/jevonian](https://github.com/xinyao27/jevonian) {{s:xinyao27/jevonian}} — Cache-aware routing that leaves the cached main chat alone.
- [miuuyy/Astra-Ares](https://github.com/miuuyy/Astra-Ares) {{s:miuuyy/Astra-Ares}} · [nidhi-singh02/agent-router](https://github.com/nidhi-singh02/agent-router) {{s:nidhi-singh02/agent-router}} · [prismhq/jev-router](https://github.com/prismhq/jev-router) {{s:prismhq/jev-router}} — Mid-run effort selection, agent/CLI selection, and a router on LiteLLM.

**Guardrails and tool-call gates.** Put deterministic rules first, and choose fail-open or fail-closed explicitly.
- [leepokai/jev-guard](https://github.com/leepokai/jev-guard) {{s:leepokai/jev-guard}} — Deny/ask/allow auto mode for any coding agent. It uses session context, flags injection in tool results, and tracks taint. [Smoke test](https://github.com/caohy1988/jev-guard-smoke).
- [DevMortimer/pi-warden](https://github.com/DevMortimer/pi-warden) {{s:DevMortimer/pi-warden}} — Steers instead of interrupting. Rule breaks fell from 6 to 0 over 150 paired runs, and a replay on 17k calls held 42.
- [thruwire/foreman](https://github.com/thruwire/foreman) {{s:thruwire/foreman}} — A supervisor for Codex and OpenCode workers, with risk-tiered thresholds.
- [jomatsu/pi-jev-auto-mode](https://github.com/jomatsu/pi-jev-auto-mode) {{s:jomatsu/pi-jev-auto-mode}} — Auto-approves Bash, write and edit calls, and **fails closed**.
- [y0usaf/pi-jev](https://github.com/y0usaf/pi-jev) {{s:y0usaf/pi-jev}} · [Nyarlathoteppppp/pi-heed](https://github.com/Nyarlathoteppppp/pi-heed) {{s:Nyarlathoteppppp/pi-heed}} · [harshwasan/jev-sentinel](https://github.com/harshwasan/jev-sentinel) {{s:harshwasan/jev-sentinel}} — Pi extensions that judge whether an action is destructive, exfiltrates data, stays in scope, or matches what you asked for.
