### Browser, desktop and mobile

The shared recipe: build a numbered list of what's on the page or screen (accessibility tree, DOM or OCR), let Jev pick the operation and target, let code execute, and call an LLM *only* when text must be typed. Hosted Jev can't see pixels.

- [browser-use/jev-ultrafast](https://github.com/browser-use/jev-ultrafast) {{s:browser-use/jev-ultrafast}} — **The most-cited project in the entire ecosystem.** It picks the operation and element in one request and booked a Zürich→London flight search in 7.1 s for $0.0039. The [launch demo](https://x.com/gregpr07/status/2100411066966749359) has been retested: 1/20 on complex tasks.
- [awlevin/typesafe-computer-use](https://github.com/awlevin/typesafe-computer-use) {{s:awlevin/typesafe-computer-use}} — macOS computer use: OCR the screen, then Jev picks the action, for ~$0.0002 per step.
- [droidrun/mobile-jev](https://github.com/droidrun/mobile-jev) {{s:droidrun/mobile-jev}} — Android automation; an Uber booking took 9 actions and ~21 s.
- [moritzkremb/jev-voice-browser](https://github.com/moritzkremb/jev-voice-browser) {{s:moritzkremb/jev-voice-browser}} — Voice control at ~300 ms per spoken word. URLs are copied from your words, never generated.
- [jkudish/jev-browser](https://github.com/jkudish/jev-browser) {{s:jkudish/jev-browser}} · [Ying-Kai-Liao/jev-browser](https://github.com/Ying-Kai-Liao/jev-browser) {{s:Ying-Kai-Liao/jev-browser}} · [wy-coliney/jev-browser-use](https://github.com/wy-coliney/jev-browser-use) {{s:wy-coliney/jev-browser-use}} — In these, the LLM plans and Jev decides. Ying-Kai-Liao's version solved 40/42 live tasks using ~70× fewer tokens.
- [Sac-Y/Jev-cu](https://github.com/Sac-Y/Jev-cu) {{s:Sac-Y/Jev-cu}} · [lahfir/agent-desktop](https://github.com/lahfir/agent-desktop) {{s:lahfir/agent-desktop}} · [savka777/jev-use](https://github.com/savka777/jev-use) {{s:savka777/jev-use}} — Desktop control through accessibility trees, with local policy gates on sensitive clicks.
- [kitze/unclutter](https://github.com/kitze/unclutter) {{s:kitze/unclutter}} · [realZachi/typesafe-adblock](https://github.com/realZachi/typesafe-adblock) {{s:realZachi/typesafe-adblock}} · [anishfn/shapeshift](https://github.com/anishfn/shapeshift) {{s:anishfn/shapeshift}} — Browser extensions and UI: clutter removal, "is this DOM element an ad?", and a text box that morphs into the UI you mean.
