### Open models and local runtimes

Independent, open alternatives, many of which serve `/v1/systemone` so the official SDK works unchanged. [The landscape and its caveats](docs/open-models.md) are covered separately.

- [NandhaKishorM/laya](https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya) {{s:NandhaKishorM/laya}} — Convai's Apache-2.0 non-autoregressive encoder (421M/322M, 100+ languages, ~33 ms). Runtimes: [laya-mlx](https://github.com/mizorewww/laya-mlx) {{s:mizorewww/laya-mlx}} (7–14 ms on M3 Max) and [receptron/laya](https://github.com/receptron/laya) {{s:receptron/laya}} (Node/ONNX).
- [jaredpalmer/kev](https://github.com/jaredpalmer/kev) {{s:jaredpalmer/kev}} — A trainable Jev-like family on Qwen3.5/3.8 with a pointer head and a `/v1/systemone` server.
- [TheoLeeCJ/SemIf-OpenJev](https://github.com/TheoLeeCJ/SemIf-OpenJev) {{s:TheoLeeCJ/SemIf-OpenJev}} — "Semantic ifs" from open models on a 3090, using shared-prefix logit readout.
- [TianyuCodings/NanoJev](https://github.com/TianyuCodings/NanoJev) {{s:TianyuCodings/NanoJev}} · [vinnylarouge/jevlike](https://github.com/vinnylarouge/jevlike) {{s:vinnylarouge/jevlike}} · [Mapika/decider](https://github.com/Mapika/decider) {{s:Mapika/decider}} · [bespokelabsai/nimble](https://github.com/bespokelabsai/nimble) {{s:bespokelabsai/nimble}} · [wfzyx/von](https://github.com/wfzyx/von) {{s:wfzyx/von}} — Trained replicas and recipes (0.4B–35B), several with published limits.
- [nokia-applied-research/AnyJev](https://github.com/nokia-applied-research/AnyJev) {{s:nokia-applied-research/AnyJev}} · [featherless-ai/simple-jev](https://github.com/featherless-ai/simple-jev) {{s:featherless-ai/simple-jev}} · [razorback16/openjev](https://github.com/razorback16/openjev) {{s:razorback16/openjev}} · [ekzhang/openjev-sglang](https://github.com/ekzhang/openjev-sglang) {{s:ekzhang/openjev-sglang}} · [githubnext/localjev](https://github.com/githubnext/localjev) {{s:githubnext/localjev}} — Turn any open LLM into a decision endpoint, with no training. AnyJev adds option-order correction.
