### Games, robotics and simulation

The recipe for games and control: feed structured state (RAM → JSON, legal-move lists), never pixels. Let code own the physics, the route and the arithmetic, and let Jev pick at branches. Keep a fast deterministic reflex layer that can veto Jev.

- [fhshaik/typesafe-mario](https://github.com/fhshaik/typesafe-mario) {{s:fhshaik/typesafe-mario}} — Super Mario Bros. from structured emulator RAM. It is the canonical "state as data" example.
- [RomanSlack/jev-drone](https://github.com/RomanSlack/jev-drone) {{s:RomanSlack/jev-drone}} — A MuJoCo drone. Jev advises at 2.5 Hz while a 50 Hz reflex layer holds a veto.
- [valentynkit/jev-plays-pokemon-red](https://github.com/valentynkit/jev-plays-pokemon-red) {{s:valentynkit/jev-plays-pokemon-red}} — Code owns the route and the arithmetic, Jev picks at branches in ~100 ms, and calibration is measured with Brier scores.
- [dabit3/jev-experiments](https://github.com/dabit3/jev-experiments) {{s:dabit3/jev-experiments}} — 22 latency-focused demo apps by Nader Dabit.
- [phyous/tsai-sc](https://github.com/phyous/tsai-sc) {{s:phyous/tsai-sc}} · [sorrycc/typesafe-snake](https://github.com/sorrycc/typesafe-snake) {{s:sorrycc/typesafe-snake}} · [standardagents/jevpilot](https://github.com/standardagents/jevpilot) {{s:standardagents/jevpilot}} · [rmalde/minecraft-agent](https://github.com/rmalde/minecraft-agent) {{s:rmalde/minecraft-agent}} — StarCraft, Snake (legal moves generated in code), a driving autopilot, and Minecraft (Astra plans, Jev acts).
- [FBddcz/embodied-jev](https://github.com/FBddcz/embodied-jev) {{s:FBddcz/embodied-jev}} · [Dimweaker/jev-libero](https://github.com/Dimweaker/jev-libero) {{s:Dimweaker/jev-libero}} · [TarunTomar122/jev-askable-arm](https://github.com/TarunTomar122/jev-askable-arm) {{s:TarunTomar122/jev-askable-arm}} · [openroboto-ai/jev-robot-control](https://github.com/openroboto-ai/jev-robot-control) {{s:openroboto-ai/jev-robot-control}} — Robot arms that pick primitives from menus, never torques. OpenRoboto compares Jev with GPT-6 Astra on cost and time.
