## Benchmarks and independent studies

Summarized with numbers in [docs/evidence.md](docs/evidence.md).

- [punk2898/awesome-jev-verified](https://github.com/punk2898/awesome-jev-verified) — **The best claim-by-claim audit.** An open 2,390-question benchmark with per-question logs, run against four GPT models. It confirms the price, but not "sub-100 ms", "445× cheaper" or "eliminates hallucination".
- [fstandhartinger/jevbench](https://github.com/fstandhartinger/jevbench) {{s:fstandhartinger/jevbench}} — JevBench: 534 frozen, half-sealed decisions and a four-axis composite across 40+ systems. See also the [Benchmark Heaven](https://benchmarkheaven.com/jev-models) leaderboard.
- [Jevals.com](https://jevals.com/) {{n:https://jevals.com}} — Jev vs six LLMs on human-labelled sets, with the data published.
- [OpenRouter: Is Jev as accurate as frontier models?](https://openrouter.ai/blog/insights/jev-vs-claude-opus-5-classification/) — Banking77: 81.0% vs Opus 5's 84.4%, at 175 ms vs 2,266 ms and $0.11 vs $2.42 per 1k.
- [willkelly/jev-evaluation](https://github.com/willkelly/jev-evaluation) {{s:willkelly/jev-evaluation}} — 123,805 pre-registered requests. ECE was 0.075 in-domain, but calibration fails OOD and authority injection works.
- [anisselbd/jev-phishing-bench](https://github.com/anisselbd/jev-phishing-bench) {{s:anisselbd/jev-phishing-bench}} — The canonical **question-atomization** lesson: 62.6% with one question vs 95.0% atomized. Haiku 4.5 wins the direct question.
- [ickma2311/jev-baselines-eval](https://github.com/ickma2311/jev-baselines-eval) {{s:ickma2311/jev-baselines-eval}} · [bitnovus/jev-spam-eval](https://github.com/bitnovus/jev-spam-eval) {{s:bitnovus/jev-spam-eval}} — Classical baselines win in-domain, but Jev wins under drift.
- [anessbelbati/jev-rerank-bench](https://github.com/anessbelbati/jev-rerank-bench) {{s:anessbelbati/jev-rerank-bench}} · [zhuyansen/jev-search-rerank-eval](https://github.com/zhuyansen/jev-search-rerank-eval) {{s:zhuyansen/jev-search-rerank-eval}} — Reranking: Jev ties Cohere, but doesn't beat embeddings alone, so fuse them.
- [jujumilk3/jev-calibration-audit](https://github.com/jujumilk3/jev-calibration-audit) {{s:jujumilk3/jev-calibration-audit}} · [KantaHayashiAI/jev-does-not-play-dice](https://github.com/KantaHayashiAI/jev-does-not-play-dice) {{s:KantaHayashiAI/jev-does-not-play-dice}} · [scienthoon/jev-ood-calibration](https://github.com/scienthoon/jev-ood-calibration) {{s:scienthoon/jev-ood-calibration}} · [jourdanlabs/assay-001](https://github.com/jourdanlabs/assay-001) {{s:jourdanlabs/assay-001}} — Calibration audits covering abstention, known probabilities, OOD, and a pre-registered test.
- [Gaurav-Gosain/jev-sec-bench](https://github.com/Gaurav-Gosain/jev-sec-bench) {{s:Gaurav-Gosain/jev-sec-bench}} · [zkousama/jagged](https://github.com/zkousama/jagged) {{s:zkousama/jagged}} — Prompt injection and vulnerable-code detection.
- [nekuda-ai/WindTunnel](https://github.com/nekuda-ai/WindTunnel) {{s:nekuda-ai/WindTunnel}} — WebMCP: Jev + Mercury solved 49/49 tasks, bare Jev 25/49.
- [Zaious/jev-capability-atlas](https://github.com/Zaious/jev-capability-atlas) {{s:Zaious/jev-capability-atlas}} · [RINNECODER/jev-behavior-study](https://github.com/RINNECODER/jev-behavior-study) {{s:RINNECODER/jev-behavior-study}} · [FirasSX914/Janus](https://github.com/FirasSX914/Janus) {{s:FirasSX914/Janus}} — Where Jev holds up vs breaks, order and lost-in-the-middle effects, and when routing is worth it.
- [thevibeworks lab](https://github.com/thevibeworks/awesome-typesafe-jev/tree/main/lab) · [rhc98 calibration report](https://github.com/rhc98/awesome-jev) · [wuyoscar evals](https://github.com/wuyoscar/jev-skill/blob/main/evals/RESULTS.md) — First-hand measurements published inside source lists.
