## Research papers

~35 Jev papers appeared within two weeks of launch, all unreplicated preprints. The full annotated list is in [docs/papers.md](docs/papers.md).

- [Jev in the Wild](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.30216) {{n:https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.30216}} — An ecosystem survey of 2,170 GitHub projects.
- [JEV-as-a-Judge](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.26550) {{n:https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.26550}} · [JEV vs. LLMs as Rubric Judges](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.29769) {{n:https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.29769}} — Jev comes within ~3 pts of GPT-6 at ~0.36% of the cost, but LLMs repeat its confident errors, which caps cascade gains.
- [Type-Safe Is Not Error-Free](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.26758) {{n:https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.26758}} · [JevOut](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.30243) {{n:https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.30243}} · [JevAdvBench](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.31142) {{n:https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.31142}} · [Decision Hijacking](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.28613) {{n:https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.28613}} — Robustness: option names, natural context and injection.
- [REFLEX](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.26532) {{n:https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.26532}} · [Jev-Mobile](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.30186) {{n:https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.30186}} · [JEV-Star](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.27331) · [Jev-Mem](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.23986) {{n:https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.23986}} — Planner/executor agents that make 66–73% fewer strong-model calls.
- [Evaluating Decision Models for Text Annotation in CSS](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.24574) · [Calibrated Decisions at Scale: crash narratives](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.24052) {{n:https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.24052}} · [Just Ask Jev](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.29429) {{n:https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.29429}} — Annotation, large-scale coding and alignment-failure detection.
- [Typed Decision Models: An Early Evidence Audit](https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.32160) — Across 28 papers there is no independent accuracy advantage; the gains are latency and cost.

